# Visual Quality & Runtime UI Inspection — {{project_name}}

<!-- GEN: Why: the agent must see the 3-step visual verification workflow, mandatory rules V1–V12, and canonical visual gate results on one screen before inspecting or grading UI screenshots. Kind: Mandatory — keep the purpose, adapt the structure (core/authoring-guide.md). -->

Open and visually inspect the rendered UI on the target platform and headless golden harness. Static analysis (`G2`) and unit/state tests (`G5`) never replace visual verification when `UI Impact: Yes`.

## 1. Visual Verification Workflow

1. **Resolve Reference & Preconditions** ([01-references-matrix-and-capture.md]({{ref_01}})):
   - Lock `REVIEW_REVISION`, target platform, flavor, entrypoint, viewports (`.superpowers/ux/viewports.json`), and data provenance (`FE_MOCKOON` vs `BE_LIVE`).
2. **Capture Runtime & Headless Golden States** ([01]({{ref_01}}), [02-headless-and-runtime-targets.md]({{ref_02}})):
   - Exercise and capture all 4 mandatory states (`Loading`, `Content`, `Empty`, `Error`) plus required orientations/themes.
   - Open and inspect every `.png` artifact directly; a saved file path alone is `UNVERIFIED`.
3. **Compare Across 10 Dimensions & Grade** ([03-comparison-checklist-and-verdict.md]({{ref_03}})):
   - Grade deviations as `BLOCKER`, `MAJOR`, `MINOR`, or `ACCEPTED (D-NN)` and record per-screen `PASS` / `FAIL` / `BLOCKED` / `NOT_RUN` / `N/A` results.

## 2. Mandatory Rules (`V1`–`V12`)

| ID | Rule | Reference |
|---|---|---|
| **V1** | **Compare against an approved reference** (extracted Figma per-screen `.png` renders + `design.md` `## UI/UX mapping`, or plan-approved baseline). | [01]({{ref_01}}) |
| **V2** | **Like-for-like matrix** (`Screen × State [Loading, Content, Empty, Error] × Viewport × Orientation`). | [01]({{ref_01}}) |
| **V3** | **Real runtime or headless golden capture** saved under the revision-bound evidence path. | [01]({{ref_01}}), [02]({{ref_02}}) |
| **V4** | **Open and inspect every image** — a file path without visual inspection is `UNVERIFIED`. | [01]({{ref_01}}), [02]({{ref_02}}) |
| **V5** | **Preserve data provenance** (`FE_MOCKOON` fixture checks vs. `BE_LIVE` integration). | [01]({{ref_01}}) |
| **V6** | **Judge by the 10 named dimensions**, never personal taste. | [03]({{ref_03}}) |
| **V7** | **Grade deviations with `BLOCKER` / `MAJOR` / `MINOR`** (`ACCEPTED (D-NN)` when covered by `D-NN`). | [03]({{ref_03}}) |
| **V8** | **Strict golden baseline governance** — never run baseline-overwrite flags during verification. | [02]({{ref_02}}) |
| **V9** | **Per-screen & per-state evidence table** with exact revision and artifact paths. | [03]({{ref_03}}) |
| **V10** | **Missing reference, target, or state is never `PASS`** (`BLOCKED` or `NOT_RUN`). | [01]({{ref_01}}), [03]({{ref_03}}) |
| **V11** | **Zero secrets or PII in screenshots** — use safe test data and redact credentials. | [01]({{ref_01}}) |
| **V12** | **Read-only inspection in Review & Verification** — return `FAIL` → `CHANGES_REQUESTED` on defects. | [03]({{ref_03}}) |

## 3. Canonical Visual Gate Results

- **`PASS`**: All required screens, 4 states, and viewports were captured, opened, and inspected on `REVIEW_REVISION` with zero `BLOCKER` or unaddressed `MAJOR` deviations.
- **`FAIL`**: Any `BLOCKER` or `MAJOR` visual deviation, layout overflow, missing state, or golden diff failure (`-> CHANGES_REQUESTED`).
- **`BLOCKED`**: Missing design reference, unavailable simulator/emulator/device, or unreachable data source.
- **`NOT_RUN`**: Required visual state or viewport was not captured.
- **`UNVERIFIED`**: Screenshot path recorded without opening and inspecting the image.
- **`N/A`**: Phase has `UI Impact: No` (with recorded reason; do not boot an emulator for non-UI work).

